<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Rehoboth Basters</h1><p class="st-meta">1870 CE – 1990 CE (approx.) · capital Rehoboth</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The self-governing community of the Rehoboth Basters in central Namibia, which kept its own captaincy and laws for more than a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Basters, descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-dutch">Cape Dutch</a> settlers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoekhoe">Khoekhoe</a> women, left the northern Cape in 1868 and under Kaptein <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermanus-van-wyk">Hermanus van Wyk</a> settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rehoboth-namibia">Rehoboth</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windhoek">Windhoek</a>, in 1870, acquiring land from the Swartbooi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 1872 they adopted written Paternal Laws, the Vaderlike Wette, establishing an elected kaptein, a Volksraad and courts. They farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and sheep, spoke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaans">Afrikaans</a> and were Lutheran Christians. A protection treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1885 preserved their autonomy, and they fought on the German side against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama</a> in 1904, but clashed with German troops at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sam-khubis">Sam Khubis</a> in 1915.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under South African rule the Basters kept partial self-government, becoming a self-governing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> in 1979. Their autonomy ended with Namibian independence in 1990, though the Kaptein's council continued to press its claims.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/rehoboth-basters.jpg" alt="Rehoboth Basters" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Bamse · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Rehoboth-Basterland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1870 CE – 1990 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rehoboth</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hermanus van Wyk, Johannes Diergaardt</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Afrikaans</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Namibia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Free Republic of Rehoboth, Rehoboth Gebiet</dd></dl></aside></div>

